<title>JAPAN: Party breakdown of Japan parliament.</title>
<headline>Party breakdown of Japan parliament.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a party breakdown of the two houses of Japan's parliament on Thursday, following the creation of the Taiyoto (Sun Party) by defectors from the main opposition Shinshinto:</p>
<p> PARTY..................Lower House....... Upper House</p>
<p> Liberal Democratic Party..238.................112</p>
<p> Shinshinto................142..................62</p>
<p> Democratic Party...........52..................14</p>
<p> Japan Communist Party......26..................14</p>
<p> Social Democratic Party....15..................29</p>
<p> Sun Party..................10...................3</p>
<p> Others......................7..................14</p>
<p> Independents...............10...................4</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Total			    500		    252</p>
<p>=================================================</p>
</text>
